.TH LT-QWWAD_EF_PARABOLIC_WELL "1" "September 2016" "lt-qwwad_ef_parabolic_well (Quantum Wells, Wires and Dots) 1.5.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lt-qwwad_ef_parabolic_well \- generate a parabolic alloy profile.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lt-qwwad_ef_parabolic_well
[\fIOPTION\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Generate a parabolic alloy profile surrounded by thick barriers.
.SH OPTIONS

Generic options:
.TP
\fB\-h\fR [ \fB\-\-help\fR ]
display a help message
.TP
\fB\-v\fR [ \fB\-\-version\fR ]
display the version of the program
.HP
\fB\-c\fR [ \fB\-\-config\fR ] arg (=qwwad.cfg) name of the configuration file to be used
.SS "Program-specific options:"
.TP
\fB\-a\fR [ \fB\-\-wellwidth\fR ] arg (=100)
Width at top of quantum well [angstrom].
.HP
\fB\-b\fR [ \fB\-\-barrierwidth\fR ] arg (=100) Width of barriers [angstrom].
.TP
\fB\-N\fR [ \fB\-\-nz\fR ] arg (=301)
Number of spatial points for output file.
.TP
\fB\-x\fR [ \fB\-\-xmin\fR ] arg (=0)
Minimum alloy fraction.
.TP
\fB\-y\fR [ \fB\-\-xmax\fR ] arg (=0.1)
Maximum alloy fraction.
.SS "Configuration options:"
.TP
\fB\-V\fR [ \fB\-\-verbose\fR ]
display lots of information about calculation
.SH FILES

.SS Output files:
   'x.r'   Alloy at each point:
           Column 1: spatial position [m].
           Column 2: alloy fraction.
.SH EXAMPLES
Generate 100-angstrom-wide parabolic-graded alloy with values ranging from 0 to 0.4, surrounded by 200-angstrom barriers:
    qwwad_ef_parabolic_well --wellwidth 100 --xmin 0 --xmax 0.4 --barrierwidth 200

Generate 100-angstrom-wide parabolic-graded alloy with values ranging from 0.1 to 0.3, surrounded by 500-angstrom barriers using 500 points in output file:
    qwwad_ef_parabolic_well --wellwidth 100 --xmin 0.1 --xmax 0.3 --barrierwidth 500 --nz 500
